  "body": "Second follow-up to #280, after #281. The re-dispatched shell build for\nv6.45.2 got further: all four legs green, the image built, the snapshot taken,\nthe volume mounted, the `.app` found, the `/Applications` symlink found — and\nthen:\n\n```\n  ok: attached read-only at /var/folders/.../volume\nDMG SMOKE FAIL: the image root is 'Applications,My Claude Code.app,', not exactly the app and the symlink\n```\n\n**The image was right. The assertion was wrong.** It compared an `LC_ALL=C`\nsorted, comma-joined listing against `\"My Claude Code.app,Applications,\"`, and\n`A` sorts before `M`. A correct artifact reported as broken is the worst way\nfor a check to fail.\n\n## The fix\n\n\"And nothing else\" is a count, not a string. The two members are already\nasserted **by name** on the two lines immediately above (`[ -d \"$app\" ]`,\n`[ -L \"$mount/Applications\" ]`, and the symlink's target). All that assertion\nhad left to say is that there is no third entry — so it counts:\n\n```bash\nentries=\"$(ls -1 \"$mount\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\"\n[ \"$entries\" -eq 2 ] || fail \"the image root has $entries entries, ...: $(ls -1 \"$mount\" | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n```\n\n`ls -1` rather than `ls -1a`: an HFS+ volume carries its own `.fseventsd` and\n`.Trashes`, which are filesystem bookkeeping rather than anything this project\nput in the image.\n\nA contract test pins the counting form, so the comparison cannot come back.\n\n## One hedge, while here\n\n`hdiutil imageinfo -format` now falls back to parsing `Format:` out of the full\nreport if the option is ever rejected, so a changed `hdiutil` CLI surface is\nnot a red release.\n\n## Progress so far, for the record\n\nThe dmg job is now proven to: download both legs' binaries, `lipo` them,\nbuild the bundle, ad-hoc sign it, verify the seal, build a UDZO HFS+ image,\nmount it read-only, and find the exact two things it should contain. What has\nnot yet run is everything from the `Info.plist` reads onward — the plist keys,\n`spctl`'s expected rejection, the quarantine handling and the launch.\n\n## Not a release\n\nNo version bump. The wheel is unaffected — v6.45.2 is published and correct.\nRe-dispatch against that tag with `-f ref=main`.",
