     "date": "2026-09-04T16:47:46Z"
    },
    "message": "Desktop shell: the dmg smoke's image-root check sorted the wrong way\n\nThe re-dispatched shell build got past the snapshot, mounted the image,\nfound the .app and found the /Applications symlink -- and then failed:\n\n    DMG SMOKE FAIL: the image root is 'Applications,My Claude Code.app,',\n    not exactly the app and the symlink\n\nThe image was right. The assertion was wrong: it compared a `LC_ALL=C\nsort`ed, comma-joined listing against \"My Claude Code.app,Applications,\",\nand `A` sorts before `M`. That is the worst way for a check to fail --\na correct artifact reported as broken.\n\n\"And nothing else\" is a count, not a string. The two members are already\nasserted by name on the two lines above; all that is left to say is that\nthere is no third, so the check counts entries instead of comparing an\norder that is a property of the locale rather than of the image. A\ncontract test pins the counting form.\n\nAlso hedged, while here: `hdiutil imageinfo -format` now falls back to\nparsing `Format:` out of the full report, so a future hdiutil that stops\naccepting the option is not a red release.\n\nNo version bump; the wheel is unaffected and v6.45.2 is published.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
